<!-- Summary Card -->
<%# `data-summary-card` IS A TEST HOOK AND IT EARNS ITS PLACE (computed-claims Task 4). This card and
    the holdings card in the right-hand column now answer the same question in the same words — what
    claims this category's spending, and what happens to it when nothing does — which is exactly the
    agreement the two are supposed to keep. Unscoped, every negative assertion about this card's
    sentence was satisfied by the OTHER card's, so a summary card serving a stale sentence out of its
    fragment cache read green. The hook is what lets the spec ask about one card. %>
<div class="bg-white shadow-sm rounded overflow-hidden border border-gray-100 p-6" data-summary-card>
  <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-4">Summary</h2>

  <% calc = category.calculator(selected_date, period: current_period) %>
  <%# ONE ARM PER CATEGORY TYPE. The cap arm that used to sit between them — a monthly budget bar,
      a pace line and a "No budget set" empty state — was deleted with the cap it read (plan 3,
      task 3). %>
  <% if category.expense? %>
    <!-- Expense Category Summary -->
    <div class="space-y-6">
      <div>
        <div class="flex justify-between text-sm mb-2">
          <span class="text-gray-500">Spent <%= period_time_label %></span>
          <span class="font-medium text-gray-900"><%= number_to_currency(calc.total_amount) %></span>
        </div>
        <%# WHAT THE SPENDING COUNTS AGAINST, IN ONE SENTENCE (computed-claims spec §3.1/§3.2).
            It named `category.pool` once and then what the category HELD, and both are gone: there
            are no pools, and nothing is held — a category's money is a claim computed from its
            rules, and spending is one of the terms that computes it (`claim = max(0, rate − spent)`
            for a rate rule; a fulfilment that drops the built-up for an accruing one). So spending
            here does not come OUT of anything, it counts AGAINST the rules that claim this
            category.

            THE OTHER ARM NAMES `free` RATHER THAN `available`. There is no available: `free` is a
            DEFINITION (`min(pot, total − Σ claims)`, §2), and a receipt no rule claims reduces it
            directly. The hero calls it "Free to spend".

            The line asks `Category#holder?`, which is the one predicate the holdings card in the
            right-hand column branches on, so the two cards on this page cannot say different things
            about the same category. %>
        <p class="text-xs text-gray-500">
          <% if category.holder? %>
            Spending here counts against what this category's rules claim
          <% else %>
            Nothing claims this category's spending — it comes straight out of what's free to spend
          <% end %>
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="border-t border-gray-200 pt-4">
        <h3 class="text-base font-medium mb-3"><%= period_trend_label %> Spending Trend</h3>
        <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded p-4 flex items-center justify-center">
          <%
            spending_data = if current_period == :ytd
                              calculate_running_total(category.entries.group_by_month(:date, range: calc.date_range).sum(:amount))
                            else
                              calculate_running_total(category.entries.group_by_day(:date, range: calc.date_range).sum(:amount))
                            end
          %>
          <%= line_chart [{ name: "Spending", data: spending_data }], curve: false, points: false, colors: [DashboardPresenter::COLORS[:brand]], prefix: "$ " %>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

  <% elsif category.income? %>
    <!-- Income Category Summary -->
    <div class="space-y-6">
      <div>
        <div class="flex justify-between text-sm mb-2">
          <span class="text-gray-500"><%= period_amount_label(:income) %></span>
          <span class="font-medium text-gray-900"><%= number_to_currency(calc.total_amount) %></span>
        </div>

        <% if current_period == :monthly %>
          <div class="flex justify-between mt-4">
            <span class="text-sm text-gray-500">vs last month</span>
            <span class="text-sm flex items-center gap-1 <%= calc.previous_month_trend == :up ? "text-status-success" : "text-status-danger" %>">
              <%= heroicon calc.previous_month_trend == :up ? "arrow-up" : "arrow-down", options: { class: "h-4 w-4" } %>
              <%= calc.previous_month_change_percentage.abs %>%
            </span>
          </div>
        <% end %>
      </div>

      <div class="border-t border-gray-200 pt-4">
        <h3 class="text-base font-medium mb-3">Income <%= current_period == :ytd ? "This Year" : "Trend" %></h3>
        <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded p-4 flex items-center justify-center">
          <%
            income_chart_range = current_period == :ytd ?
              calc.date_range :
              (selected_date.beginning_of_month - 5.months)..selected_date.end_of_month
          %>
          <%= line_chart category.entries.group_by_month(:date, range: income_chart_range).sum(:amount), curve: false, points: false, colors: [DashboardPresenter::COLORS[:brand]], prefix: "$ " %>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    
  <%# THE SAVINGS ARM IS DELETED (plan 3, task 5) — a "Monthly Contribution" figure, a pool box
      saying "This category contributes to a shared goal", and a running-total line drawn by
      `CategoriesHelper#savings_evolution_series` (deleted with it, one reader). There is no savings
      TYPE: a goal is an ordinary expense category that names a target, and what it has saved is a
      claim its rules have built up toward that figure (computed-claims spec §3.2). The holdings
      card in the right-hand column is where that is read. %>
  <% end %>
</div> 